At line 895-899:
```rust
PendingTrigger::EnteredBattlefield { object_id, card_id, .. } => {
    // Verify the object is still on the battlefield.
    if state.get_object(object_id).map(|o| o.zone == Zone::Battlefield).unwrap_or(false) {
        if let Some(behavior) = registry.get(card_id) {
            behavior.on_enter_battlefield(state, object_id, registry);
        }
    }
}
```

So when an `EnteredBattlefield` trigger resolves, it:


1. Checks if the object is still on the battlefield
2. If yes, calls `on_enter_battlefield`

Mirror-Mad Phantasm has no `on_enter_battlefield` override (CardBehavior default implementation), so this is a no-op. That's correct.

But I'm noticing something odd at line 349 - the comment says "Only collect if the card has an on_enter_battlefield handler," but the actual check at line 351 just verifies the card exists in the registry with `registry.get(card_id).is_some()`. That's always true for valid cards, so the comment is misleading - every card that enters the battlefield gets an ETB trigger collected regardless of whether it actually has a handler.

Most cards just no-op when these triggers resolve since the default `on_enter_battlefield` implementation does nothing, so it's not a correctness issue for Mirror-Mad Phantasm, just a minor inefficiency.

Now let me trace what happens when the phantasm leaves the battlefield during ability activation - a `LeftBattlefield` event fires, so I need to check what triggers get collected from that.

